    description: "INV-dihos Phase 3 (split): Return-Type Registry — Scala portion.\n\nWI-titor was originally scoped to ship Rust + C++ + Scala in one PR. Per\nthe WI's own splitting hint (\"consider splitting if it grows too large to\nship as a single PR\"), the Rust slice landed first as a standalone PR\n(see WI-titor pr_ref). This sibling WI tracks the Scala slice.\n\nDELIVERABLES:\n(1) Extend the existing Scala var_types infrastructure (scala.py:613-647\n    already has constructor + parameter tracking) to consult the\n    method-return-type registry for chained method calls. Smaller\n    delta than C++ / Rust because the bootstrap already exists —\n    closer to the Phase 2 (WI-jujup) shape.\n\n(2) Populate `FileAnalysis.method_return_types` from each\n    function_definition's signature in Pass 1.\n\n(3) Tier 2 escape hatches in a `_extract_scala_return_type_name` helper:\n    - basic return-type extraction from `def f(...): T = ...` shape\n    - generic strip: `List[T]` / `Map[K, V]` → `List` / `Map` (Scala\n      uses `[T]` not `<T>`)\n    - smart-pointer-equivalent unwrap: `Option[T]` / `Try[T]` /\n      `Future[T]` / `Either[L, R]` (right-biased) — analogous to Rust\n      `Option<T>` / `Result<T, E>`\n    - implicits explicitly deferred per the original WI-titor text\n      (\"Scala implicits left as future work\")\n\n(4) Wire registry into Pass 2 var_types fill loop + add new\n    resolution strategy in `_extract_edges_scala` for typed-variable\n    method calls (mirror Rust's Strategy 1.8).\n\n(5) Regression tests per language. Target a bakeoff repo with active\n    receiver-type-blocked dispatch: any Spark/Akka Scala monorepo per\n    ADR-0006 §Phase rollout.\n\nPREREQUISITE: WI-titor (Rust slice) landed — pattern established in\n`base.py` §4c aggregation + `_extract_var_types_*` per-language helper\nconvention.\n\nTag at merge: `awaits_bakeoff_validation`."  # ea5c
    fields: {}  # ea5c
